Phase 1 verification and checkpoint (Track foundation-core_20260918)

Automated checks, all run with the commands recorded in the process document:
- Core test suite: ran clean, exit status zero. No core modules exist yet, so
  the suite is empty by design; the runner's failure path was proved separately
  with a temporary failing test when it was built.
- Linter: two files, no warnings, no errors.
- Formatter: whole tree clean.
- Real runtime: a batch run inside the application confirmed the registered
  command is callable and an invented command name is not, which proves both
  the extension's startup function and its command registration.

Visual verification, performed by driving the running application rather than
asking a person:
- The application was launched, its File menu opened with a keyboard shortcut,
  and the window captured. The extension's own group appears in that menu.
- Navigating into the group and activating its single entry produced the
  expected box with the expected two lines, and no permission prompt appeared -
  which is the specific friction this project set out to avoid.
- One defect was found this way and fixed inside the phase: the box named the
  wrong menu path for where the tools live. The group sits directly in the File
  menu as a sibling of the scripts submenu, not nested inside it as assumed.
  The corrected text was verified the same way.

Environment work done alongside the phase, at the operator's request:
- The editor was installed as a normal desktop application: binary linked onto
  the path, icons in five sizes, a validated desktop entry, the sprite file type
  associated, and a thumbnail generator limited to sprite files only rather than
  taking over every common image format as the upstream script would have.

Phase outcome: the skeleton, the tooling, the test harness and the proof that a
command reaches the running application are all in place. The mathematical core
itself is the next phase's work.
